# Moddy Arena: a fighter knocked out in a battle comes back in the prep room even when his own respawn point is far
# away (as a bed would be: here a point set by command, 300 blocks off), keeps his place in the battle and is taken
# back in (before, he woke at his point and the battle counted him as having left: out for good with lives left).
# The arena only moves that one respawn and saves nothing: his point is still his afterwards (Moddy-Worlds#60).
# play-timeout: 600
@intent a fighter whose respawn point is far from the arena comes back in the prep room when knocked out in a battle and stays in it, and his own respawn point is never changed
@world flat seed=1
@continue-on-fail

@step arrive, with his respawn point far away
@expect chat Welcome to Moddy Arena within 90s
@wait 2s
difficulty hard
difficulty normal
gamemode survival
effect give @s minecraft:resistance 600 4 true
# his respawn point: a stone pad high above the ground 300 blocks off (as a bed would be)
forceload add 0 320 2 322
@wait 2s
fill 0 120 320 2 120 322 minecraft:stone
spawnpoint @s 1 121 321
@wait 1s

@step knocked out in wave 1, back in the prep room with lives left, and taken back in
moddy arena start
@expect title Wave 1 of 5 within 20s
@wait 1s
kill @s
@expect chat Knocked out! 2 lives left within 10s
@wait 1s
effect give @s minecraft:resistance 600 4 true
@assert execute if entity @s[x=-4,y=63,z=17,dx=8,dy=3,dz=8]
@expect actionbar Back into the arena in 1 within 10s
@wait 2s
@assert execute if entity @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]
@assert execute unless entity @s[x=-50,y=-64,z=100,dx=100,dy=400,dz=400]
@shot back-in-after-a-knock-out

@step out of lives the battle is lost, and he watches from the prep room
kill @s
@expect chat Knocked out! 1 life left within 10s
@wait 2s
kill @s
@expect chat no lives left within 10s
@wait 1s
@assert execute if entity @s[x=-4,y=63,z=17,dx=8,dy=3,dz=8]
@expect chat The arena is tidy again within 30s

@step after the battle his own respawn point is still his
# the arena saved nothing: the point he set is kept, untouched by three knock-outs. (Where he wakes after the battle
# is the core's rule for a world with bases: in the arena world every player's base is the place, so a respawn away
# from it is sent home. In an arena built in another world it is his own point again.)
@assert execute if data entity @s respawn{pos:[I;1,121,321]}
@wait 2s
kill @s
@wait 3s
@assert execute if data entity @s respawn{pos:[I;1,121,321]}
